From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-pci-renesas - keep RAM firmware controllers out of D3cold

Since 7.3 the DWC host powers the link off in system suspend once every
endpoint is in D3hot. A uPD720201 without a ROM loses the firmware the
driver uploaded at probe, so resume times out ("Controller not ready")
and the HC dies. Mark such controllers no_d3cold and make the host check
honour it.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@
 	if (!pdev->dev.driver && !pci_is_enabled(pdev))
 		return 0;
 
-	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot)
+	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot || pdev->no_d3cold)
 		goto exit;
 
 	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev)) {
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci-renesas.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci-renesas.c
@@ -636,6 +636,10 @@
 	if (retval)
 		return retval;
 
+	/* Without a ROM the firmware is in RAM and does not survive D3cold */
+	if (!renesas_check_rom(dev))
+		pci_d3cold_disable(dev);
+
 	return xhci_pci_common_probe(dev, id);
 }
 
